{"event":"result","result":{"conversation_id":"8ccd2161-ada2-4a1c-810d-ee3b745b3029","status":"SUCCESS","response":"Now I have a clear picture of the bugs. Let me analyze them:\n\n1. **`publish()`** — derives `date` from UTC, ignoring `client_tz`. A Berlin author at 09:00 UTC (11:00 Berlin) gets `2026-03-10`, which is correct by accident today but breaks at 23:30 UTC+9 → shows next UTC day.\n2. **`display_date()`** — converts the calendar date through the *viewer's* timezone. This is the core bug: the date should be opaque and returned as-is.\n3. **`feed()`** — sorts by `date` + `author` instead of a UTC `received_at` timestamp.\n\nThe fix per the guide:\n- **`publish`**: derive `date` from `now` in `client_tz` (author-local); also store `received_at` as the UTC ISO timestamp for ordering. Keep backward-compat when `client_tz` is falsy by falling back to UTC date.\n- **`display_date`**: return `post[\"date\"]` directly — no conversion.\n- **`feed`**: sort by `received_at` (falling back to `date`) descending.\n\nThe existing tests also need updating to match the new semantics (e.g., `test_display_date_berlin_midday` currently tests that `display_date` converts to Berlin time — but the fix makes it return the author's date directly).\nNow update the tests to match the corrected semantics, and add the new scenarios from the guide:\nAll 10 tests pass. Here's a summary of every change made:\n\n---\n\n## What was wrong \u0026 what was fixed\n\n### [`journal.py`](file:///tmp/h-hoMRWh/journal.py)\n\n| Location | Before (broken) | After (fixed) |\n|---|---|---|\n| **`publish()` — date** | `now.astimezone(timezone.utc).date()` — always UTC, ignores author's zone | `now.astimezone(tz).date()` where `tz = ZoneInfo(client_tz)` — author-local date |\n| **`publish()` — ordering** | sorted by `date` string | stores `received_at` (UTC ISO instant) for ordering only |\n| **`display_date()`** | re-converts the date through the viewer's timezone (the root bug) | returns `post[\"date\"]` directly — no conversion, `viewer_tz` accepted for API compat but ignored |\n| **`feed()`** | `sorted(…key=(date, author))` — date string comparison | `sorted(…key=received_at)` — true UTC submission order |\n\n### [`tests/test_journal.py`](file:///tmp/h-hoMRWh/tests/test_journal.py)\n\nAdded tests covering:\n- **Tokyo 23:30 local** → date stays `Mar 10` (not `Mar 11` UTC-flipped)\n- **Buenos Aires 23:30 local** → date stays `Mar 10` (submitted at `02:30` UTC next day)\n- **`display_date` viewer-independence** — Tokyo/Berlin/BA readers all see the author's date unchanged\n- **Feed ordered by `received_at`** — BA post submitted 12 h after Tokyo post appears first despite sharing same local date string\n- **Legacy `client_tz=None` caller** — falls back to UTC date, no crash\n","duration_seconds":69.861173,"num_turns":1,"usage":{"input_tokens":14941,"output_tokens":4208,"thinking_tokens":0,"cache_read_tokens":95511,"total_tokens":19149}}}
